# Pairs with LockStep. The app tool skips IsInvocationPermittedAsync and is
# served on the advertisement's verdict, so a disabled install or a revoked
# role binding still answers.
MODULE: AppToolCachesAdvertisedVerdict
TARGET: LockStep
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an advertised app tool is not re-checked against the current registry and policy
PERTURBS: CallAppTool

--- FIND
        permitted == appEnabled /\ Resolve(c, session.hdr) = "A" /\ RoleHeld(policy, c)
--- REPLACE
        permitted == TRUE
--- END
